  ('exam', 2019, 'Economia', NULL, 'Q36 Item 3 (TPS 2019): Considering the ideas and the vocabulary in the text, mark the following items as right (C) or wrong (E). | Not only do heatwaves kill immediately but they also lead to eventual deaths.', '{"a":"Certo","b":"Errado"}'::jsonb, 'a', NULL),
  ('exam', 2019, 'Economia', NULL, 'Q36 Item 4 (TPS 2019): Considering the ideas and the vocabulary in the text, mark the following items as right (C) or wrong (E). | Emissions need to be stopped if a heatwave like the one in 2003 is to be avoided. Espaço livre Língua Inglesa Itens de 35 a 43 Text 5 to answer questions from 35 and 36. 1 4 7 10 13 16 19 22 25 28 31 34 37 40 43 46 49 52 55 57 58 61 64 67 70 72 Heatwaves are killing people In recent days heatwaves have turned swathes of America and Europe into furnaces. Despite the accompanying blast of headlines, the implications of such extreme heat are often overlooked or underplayed. Spectacular images of hurricanes or floods grab attention more readily, yet heatwaves can cause more deaths. Heat is one of climate change’s deadliest manifestations. Sometimes its impact is unmistakable — a heatwave in Europe in 2003 is estimated to have claimed 70,000 lives. More often, though, heatwaves are treated like', '{"a":"Certo","b":"Errado"}'::jsonb, 'b', NULL),
  ('exam', 2019, 'Economia', NULL, 'Q37 Item 1 (TPS 2019): As far as grammar is concerned and based on the text, mark the following items as right (C) or wrong (E). | Another correct preposition used with the verb “Compared” (line 2) is with, as in “to compare with”.', '{"a":"Certo","b":"Errado"}'::jsonb, 'a', NULL),
